WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:03.620
When it comes to DC movies, we have questions.

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:05.180
Just what is going on with the Joker?

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:06.940
What's going to happen with Harley Quinn?

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:09.520
And where is the DCEU actually headed?

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:13.740
Well, nobody's really got any answers to all
that, but it's not for lack of trying.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:17.820
Here are a few DC movie theories that, if
true, would change everything.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:22.560
Over the last few decades, the Joker has become
one of the world's best-known baddies.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:26.779
So it's no wonder that DC is tryingtheir best
to get the most out of one of their most iconic

00:00:26.779 --> 00:00:31.199
characters — namely by producing not one,
but two Joker-centric films.

00:00:31.199 --> 00:00:35.649
Of course, first there's Joker, the award-winning,
R-rated take on a failed comedian becoming

00:00:35.649 --> 00:00:40.720
the grease-painted face of an anarchist movement,
starring the frankly astonishing Joaquin Phoenix.

00:00:40.829 --> 00:00:45.060
But then you've got the controversial Joker
from Suicide Squad - a slightly more modern,

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:48.260
tatted-up version, performed by a husky-voiced
Jared Leto.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:51.420
But are these two Jokers in the same cinematic
universe?

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:52.360
And if so, how?

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:53.640
Which is the real Joker?

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:57.980
Well, one popular theory claims that they're
both Jokers, with the Joker being more of

00:00:57.980 --> 00:00:59.660
an idea than a single person.

00:01:00.069 --> 00:01:04.839
Specifically, some fans believe that Leto's
Joker was at one time Jason Todd, one of Batman's

00:01:04.839 --> 00:01:09.130
own Robins - before he was brutalized and
brainwashed by a previous Clown Prince of

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:10.130
Crime.

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:13.950
That would handily explain the memorialized
armor in the Batcave reading, "Ha ha ha, joke's

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:14.860
on you, Batman."

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:16.940
"And I thought my jokes were bad."

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:22.060
Of course, it's also possible Joker truly
is a standalone film, with no connection whatsoever

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:23.620
to the wider DCEU.

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:24.980
But that's less fun, isn't it?

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:29.680
DC has agotten something of a bad rap for
making their movies just a little too gritty

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:30.180
and dark.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:35.040
But Joker has fully embraced the much-lampooned
edginess of DC, creating a film that goes

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:37.580
where no superhero film has dared to go before.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.820
This formula appears to be successful, too.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:44.380
Joaquin Phoenix's performance has been praised
left and right, and Joker has won all sorts

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:45.590
of accolades and awards.

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:51.119
In fact, rumor has it that Joker is just the
first of DC's Black, a new label for DC movies

00:01:51.119 --> 00:01:55.950
that exist outside the DCEU as we know it
- and which are somehow even darker than the

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:58.520
already grim and gritty films of the DCEU.

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:04.160
Back in 2017, writer Mark Millar tweeted to
director Jordan Vogt-Roberts that DC was pitching

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:07.760
directors for an adaptation of the comic storyline
Superman: Red Son.

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:11.880
This alternate timeline imagines what would
happen if Superman had landed in the Soviet

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:13.330
Union rather than Kansas.

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:17.560
In case you're wondering, Superman fighting
for Stalin rather than the American Way turns

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:21.240
the Cold War into a superhuman arms race,
rather than a nuclear one.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:26.090
Such a dark and politically charged plot seems
tailor made for a DC Dark label, and with

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:29.580
Joker's recent successes, there's a chance
we could see it hit screens soon.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:35.260
According to the teaser trailer for the action-packed,
gritty girl power film Birds of Prey, Harley

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:37.120
Quinn is kinda over clowns.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:41.360
And the film's subtitle, And the Fantabulous
Emancipation of One Harley Quinn, would seem

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:41.980
to say it all.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:46.390
Harley is done with being the Joker's minion,
so she finally cuts ties with the Clown Prince

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:46.940
of Crime.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:51.040
She's doing her own thing, with her own friends
- namely a bunch of super-powered women who

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:54.620
want to protect a young girl from Black Mask,
a vicious crime lord.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:56.660
"We're bad guys.

00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:57.860
It's what we do."

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:02.700
The first of a proposed trilogy, these films
will bring to life some of Gotham's favorite

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:05.460
femme fatales - one of whom could well be
Poison Ivy.

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:10.320
The potential introduction of Poison Ivy into
the DCEU has comic fans excited about what

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:11.280
it could mean for Harley.

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:16.460
After her big breakup with Mr. J in the comics,
Harley finds love and support in a new relationship

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:17.000
with Ivy.

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:20.840
Margot Robbie herself has even said that their
intimate relationship was one of her favorite

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:24.640
parts of the comics - and something she hopes
to explore in future films.

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:30.331
Before fans dive into Atlantis once more for
the DCEU's second Aquaman film, they'll be

00:03:30.331 --> 00:03:33.960
taking a detour a little further down: deep
into the Trench.

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:39.150
One of the scariest scenes in a DC film so
far, James Wan's 2018 blockbuster features

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:43.260
a moment where Arthur and Mera barely make
it of the terrifying depths of the Trench.

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:47.760
Now, Warner Brothers are giving the DC Universe
its first true horror movie, set to take place

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:50.240
among the many sharp-toothed creatures of
the Trench.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:54.190
With a Trench spinoff in the works, fans are
wondering if Wan will do for Aquaman what

00:03:54.190 --> 00:03:55.880
he did for The Conjuring universe.

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:59.980
What started with just a single film in that
world quickly blossomed into many, including

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:03.120
Anabelle, The Nun, and The Curse of La Llorona,
to name a few.

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:07.340
Similarly, some are hoping for the gradual
development of a kind of Aquaman Cinematic

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:11.300
Universe, with fans theorizing that The Trench
will be the first of many films that will

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:12.960
explore the undersea world.

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:17.860
Most of the Justice League members have gotten
their own movies by now, so when will it finally

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:19.220
be Barry Allen's turn?

00:04:19.329 --> 00:04:23.400
Well, it's been long confirmed that there
is a solo Flash flick in the works, but due

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:27.139
to creative differences and Ezra Miller's
packed schedule, it's gotten caught up in

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:27.960
development hell.

00:04:28.169 --> 00:04:32.139
But maybe that's for the best, since according
to Miller, the Flash film will see the DCEU

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:33.280
"torn asunder."

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:36.500
But maybe the DCEU getting torn a new one
might be a good thing.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:40.879
The Flash will apparently be centered around
the Flashpoint storyline, in which Barry creates

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:44.560
an alternate timeline by going back in the
past in order to save his mother.

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:47.500
But this new reality is kinda messed up, to
say the least.

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:52.680
Fans have suggested that the topsy-turvy universe
created by Flashpoint would be a logical explanation

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:56.560
for the establishment for an Elseworlds or
DC Dark series of films.

00:04:56.640 --> 00:05:00.840
Others, meanwhile, have said that this adaptation
of Flashpoint will serve as a hard reboot

00:05:00.850 --> 00:05:05.129
for the whole of the DCEU, giving Warner Brothers
the chance to start anew.

00:05:05.129 --> 00:05:09.210
This would easily explain the existence of
the upcoming new Robert Pattinson Batman,

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:13.080
as well as a new Superman, should Henry Cavill
decide to hang up the cape for good.

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:17.160
One thing is for sure: while other cinematic
universes have entered the Endgame, things

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:19.140
are just getting started for DC.

